  "user_request_original": "Design a 21-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 Fabry-Perot bandpass filter on Fused Silica substrate under normal incidence. Layer sequence from air: Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5. Initialize all 21 layers at thicknesses: [176.44, 391.04, 313.22, 261.55, 173.42, 302.83, 187.13, 192.43, 217.30, 235.01, 223.53, 231.35, 136.74, 209.72, 419.02, 311.39, 164.85, 233.44, 201.70, 302.14, 167.43] nm. Freeze layers 0-6 and 12-20 (indices) at these values. Optimize only layers 7, 8, 9, 10, 11 with bounds 50-450 nm using gradient_thickness optimizer with maximum step size 0.05 nm per iteration. Evaluate coherent TMM transmittance across 1300-1800 nm. Score: maximize T at 1550 nm, minimize T in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize the thickness of the five central layers in a 21-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 Fabry-Perot filter on fused silica to maximize transmittance at 1550 nm and suppress transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm across 1300-1800 nm at normal incidence.",
